a346a2d380"},{"text":"Some women were physically incapable, and the guys would say, “See, I told you women can′t hack it.” The more I saw of that, the more pissed I got, and the more determined I got to stick it out.","ref":"1989, Judith Stiehm, Arms And The Enlisted Woman, page 255:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[134,140]],"id":"2f30cbef-1d10-4e3f-a2ce-e58500069f9c"},{"text":"So I was already pissed at Bill to begin with, for what happened with the O′Donnell disaster the year before, and now I was even more pissed at the fuckin′ guy.","ref":"2009, Steve Serby, No Substitute for Sundays: Brett Favre and His Year in the Huddle with the New York Jets, page xv:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[17,23],[134,140]],"id":"3221700b-8f02-4207-b4c0-249f73351138"}],"categories":["American English","Australian English","Canadian English","English colloquialisms","English terms with quotations","English vulgarities"],"links":[["Annoyed","annoyed"],["angry","angry"]],"raw_glosses":["(chiefly US, Canada, Australia, mildly vulgar, colloquial) Annoyed, angry."],"glosses":["Annoyed, angry."],"tags":["Australia","Canada","US","colloquial","mildly","vulgar"],"id":"0b76db83-b930-4a14-aa6d-2a6496a0b9a0"}],"related":[{"tags":["noun"],"word":"piss-up"}],"synonyms":[{"sense":"drunk","word":"drunk"},{"word":"pissed drunk"},{"word":"intoxicated"},{"word":"bladdered"},{"word":"blotto"},{"word":"plastered"},{"word":"rat-arsed"},{"word":"drunk"},{"sense":"annoyed, angry","word":"pissed off"},{"word":"angry"}]},"pistil":{"id":"bb7004c4-3555-48f5-8a97-1225d987f062","word":"pistil","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a discrete unit in the center of a flower which receives the pollen and produces a fruit","tags":["masculine"],"word":"pistilo"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Some plant species have more than one pistil per flower.","bold_text_offsets":[[38,44]],"type":"example","id":"3a299355-2e6a-4e26-9fc1-a3726c5941b2"}]